WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Raj: We're seeing intermittent failures in zone A. Zone B's samples are clean so far.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:13.080
Hannah: Are all A hosts using the same resolver? Check the effective client settings.

3
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.440
Anika: Affected clients point to resolver A. That's our blast radius so far, not the whole region.

4
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:26.976
Priya: Just to confirm, one successful lookup doesn't clear A, right? We need repeated samples.

5
00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:32.280
Lukas: Right. A cached result could succeed while fresh requests still fail.

6
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:38.712
Raj: I'm on it. I'll record failures and timings, not just the final answer.

7
00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:45.120
Hannah: I'll keep an eye on B too. A few clean samples aren't a complete health check.

8
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:52.272
Anika: Payments itself responds over established connections. We can rule that out as a total outage.

9
00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:58.488
Lukas: Good distinction. That doesn't rule out every payment issue, just a complete outage.

10
00:00:58.488 --> 00:01:05.880
Priya: Okay. Keep the scope precise. Let's compare A and B from the same client next.

